/**
@page building Building, testing and consuming

@section build_deps Dependencies

- CMake ≥ 3.26 and a C++23 compiler (GCC ≥ 13 or Clang ≥ 17)
- Boost ≥ 1.74 (header-only use: Boost.Odeint)
- Blaze ≥ 3.8

The test suite uses Catch2 v3, found via `find_package` or fetched
automatically with FetchContent. Nothing else — no BLAS/LAPACK/TBB.

@section build_build Building

@code{.sh}
cmake --preset release
cmake --build --preset release
./build/release/bin/ctr_demo
@endcode

Presets: `dev` (Debug + warnings), `dev-asan` (+ Address/UB sanitizers),
`release`, `release-native` (`-march=native` + LTO), `bench` (benchmarks).

Options: `CTR_ENABLE_WARNINGS`, `CTR_WARNINGS_AS_ERRORS`,
`CTR_ENABLE_SANITIZERS`, `CTR_ENABLE_NATIVE`, `CTR_ENABLE_LTO`,
`CTR_BUILD_EXAMPLES`, `CTR_BUILD_BENCHMARKS`, `CTR_BUILD_DOCS`.

@section build_test Testing

@code{.sh}
ctest --preset release             # everything
ctest --preset release -L unit     # fast unit tests
ctest --preset release -LE slow    # skip the convergence study
@endcode

The regression suite includes golden forward-kinematics values, analytic
anchors (straight-tube, planar arc-chain, twist-rate identity, rotational
equivariance), solver cross-validation, Jacobian-vs-central-difference
checks and FK → IK → FK round trips.

@section build_bench Benchmarks

@code{.sh}
cmake --preset bench && cmake --build --preset bench
./build/bench/bin/ctr_benchmarks
@endcode

@section build_consume Consuming the library

Installed package:

@code{.sh}
cmake --install build/release --prefix /your/prefix
@endcode

@code{.cmake}
find_package(ctr_kinematics CONFIG REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(your_app PRIVATE ctr::kinematics)
@endcode

Or vendored: `add_subdirectory(Concentric-Tube-Robot)` provides the same
`ctr::kinematics` target.

@section build_docs Documentation

@code{.sh}
doxygen docs/Doxyfile        # output in docs/generated/html
@endcode

or configure with `-DCTR_BUILD_DOCS=ON` and build the `ctr_docs` target.
*/
